    "summary_one_sentence": "In 2025 Madrid, a filmmaker undergoing a creative block writes an autofictional screenplay about an overworked commercial director who flees to the Canary Islands following a panic attack.",
    "summary_short": "Struggling with creative block in 2025, director Raúl attempts to break his drought by crafting an autofictional screenplay centered on his female alter ego, Elsa. Set in 2004, Elsa's story follows an unsuccessful movie director turned ad director who buries her grief after her mother's death under relentless work. When severe panic attacks force her to halt production, she leaves her supportive partner behind in Madrid to seek solace in the Canary Islands. As Raúl weaves Elsa’s journey with his own life in the present, the film explores the fine line separating reality, memory, and artistic creation.",
    "summary_long": "In 2025 Spain, acclaimed filmmaker Raúl finds himself stuck in a severe creative rut while attempting to conceive his next project. To overcome his mental blockage, he turns to autofiction and begins writing a screenplay set during the December holidays of 2004. His fictional narrative centers on Elsa, a former feature filmmaker who shifted to directing commercial advertisements after early career setbacks. When Elsa's mother passes away, she submerges herself in her demanding job to avoid confronting her overwhelming grief. However, suppressing her emotions leads to crippling panic attacks and physical exhaustion, forcing her to temporarily halt her work. With the gentle encouragement of her patient partner Bonifacio, Elsa decides to step away from Madrid and retreat to the volcanic landscapes of Lanzarote. Joined by her close friend Patricia, Elsa uses her time on the Canary Islands to heal, reflect, and gradually rediscover her passion for cinema. Back in 2025, Raúl’s process of writing Elsa's journey begins to deeply intertwine with his own romantic and professional life in Madrid. He draws heavy inspiration from his partner and inner circle, constantly blurring the boundary between his reality and the art he creates. Ultimately, the film serves as a poignant exploration of loss, creative revival, and the healing power of storytelling.",
    "synopsis": "Bitter Christmas (Amarga Navidad) is a multi-layered tragicomedy that examines the intimate relationship between artistic inspiration, personal grief, and healing. Set across dual timelines, the story anchors itself in 2025 with Raúl, a celebrated filmmaker navigating a prolonged spell of creative drought. In an effort to reignite his imagination, Raúl dives into writing an autofictional narrative set in 2004. His protagonist, Elsa, is a once-promising director turned ad maker who throws herself into relentless work to mask her grief following her mother’s death. When severe panic attacks force Elsa to stop, she escapes to Lanzarote in the Canary Islands with a close friend, leaving her supportive partner behind in Madrid as she attempts to reclaim her artistic voice. As Raúl writes, the boundaries between his own reality in Madrid and Elsa’s fictional journey begin to dissolve, offering a thoughtful and humorous meditation on the limits of autofiction and the emotional costs of creation.",
